# Everything this directory produces, refused by name rather than by pattern, so
# a new output has to be thought about rather than silently ignored.
#
# `authority.crt` is a public certificate and would be harmless to commit; it is
# refused anyway, because a repository that carries an authority's certificate
# is one pull request away from carrying its key, and the reader who trusts one
# has no way to tell which they were handed. `generate.sh` explains the grant.
authority.crt
authority.p12
chain.crt
keycloak.crt
keycloak.p12
